<Project>

  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!-- Everything under tests/ is a test project; the shared test settings live in the root Directory.Build.targets. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <!--
      Zero-allocation gates measure GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread over a window; tiered recompilation
      (OSR, PGO instrumentation) inside that window allocates and made them flake under the parallel
      whole-solution run. Every test project runs fully optimised code from the first call (TASK-42; it used to
      be set per project and Colony.Testing.Tests, Fields, Generated and ProcGen lacked it).
    -->
    <TieredCompilation>false</TieredCompilation>
    <TieredPGO>false</TieredPGO>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
